Café 1959's José Giraldo Natural Papayo Coffee offers a captivating tropical symphony in each cup, with vibrant aromas of papaya and mango, bright acidity, and intense red fruit sweetness, leading to a sparkling, elegant finish that lingers on the palate.&nbsp;

The Papayo variety, an Ethiopian Landrace, features distinctive elongated cherries that resemble papaya fruit. Grown by third-generation coffee producer José Giraldo at Finca Las Marias in Pijao, Quindio, Colombia, this coffee is a testament to José's commitment to innovation and excellence.

